that would be rkward 0.4.9c. That release dates from March 2010, but active 
development of this series of rkward stopped in late 2007. This works with KDE 
3.x. Last version of R this is known to work with is 2.10.0, although with 
luck, it *might* work with some versions of R after this (but definitely not R 
2.14.0 or above). I don't know for sure, because nobody tested this, because 
this version of rkward is totally obsolete.

Seriously: Just post the exact cmake command you were using, and even more 
importantly, the *exact* output you got. Chances are, we'll be able to provide 
you with a solution in less than 24 hours, including the lag due to different 
time zones.

(But in fact, my next guess is that you simply gave cmake the path to the 
"rkward"-subdirectory, instead of to the toplevel directory of the sources. In 
the development version of rkward, I have already added a check for this 
condition, and a better error message. See: We *do* care about such problems.)

